String.intern()` behavior version-wise

🔹 What is `String.intern()`?
    👉 `intern()` returns a reference from the String Constant Pool (SCP).
    * If the string already exists in SCP → returns existing reference
    * If not present → adds it to SCP and returns reference

🔹 Behavior BEFORE Java 7 (Java 6 and earlier)
    📍 Where was SCP?
    ➡️ PermGen
    🔹 intern() behavior
        * Creates a NEW copy of the string in SCP (PermGen)
        * Even if the string existed in Heap, a new object was created

        Example (Java ≤ 6)
        String s1 = new String("Java");
        String s2 = s1.intern();
        System.out.println(s1 == s2); // false
        
        Memory diagram
        
        Heap
        ┌───────────────────┐
        │ new String("Java")│ ◄─ s1
        └───────────────────┘
        PermGen (SCP)
        ┌─────────────┐
        │ "Java"      │ ◄─ s2 (new copy)
        └─────────────┘
        
        ✔ Two different objects
        ❌ Extra memory usage

🔹 Behavior AFTER Java 7 (Java 7, 8, 11, 17…)
     📍 Where is SCP?
    ➡️ Heap
     🔹 intern() behavior
        * No new copy is created
        * If SCP doesn’t have it → heap object reference is reused
        * More memory efficient

        🔹Example 1: intern after Java 7

        String s1 = new String("Java");
        String s2 = s1.intern();
        System.out.println(s1 == s2); // true

        Memory diagram

        Heap
        ┌────────────────────────────┐
        │ String Constant Pool       │
        │                            │
        │ new String("Java") ◄─ s1,s2│
        └────────────────────────────┘

        ✔ Same object reused
        ✔ No duplicate object

        🔹 Example 2: Literal first, then intern

        String s1 = "Hello";
        String s2 = new String("Hello");
        String s3 = s2.intern();

        System.out.println(s1 == s3); // true
        System.out.println(s2 == s3); // false

         Explanation
        * `"Hello"` already exists in SCP
        * `intern()` returns SCP reference


        🔹 Example 3: Runtime string creation

        String s1 = new String("Hel") + new String("lo");
        String s2 = s1.intern();
        String s3 = "Hello";

        System.out.println(s1 == s2); // true (Java 7+)
        System.out.println(s2 == s3); // true

         Why?
        * `"Hello"` not in SCP before `intern()`
        * Heap object is added to SCP

